Source: linscp
Section: net
Maintainer: Eduardo Correia <ecorreia@apliant.com.br>
# clang, not GCC: the core's VCL property shim needs __declspec(property)
# (-fms-extensions), which GCC does not implement; CMakeLists.txt stops the
# configure step with any other compiler. clang is used for C too, so that
# every translation unit shares the same -fshort-wchar ABI.
# The linker is the default one (GNU ld): lld is only used by the Windows
# cross-build.
# python3: the build transforms the upstream tree (port/tools/transform.py).
# No perl: it is only for the bundled OpenSSL's Configure, and the package
# uses the system OpenSSL and expat.
Build-Depends:
 clang,
 cmake (>= 3.25),
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 libexpat1-dev (>= 2.4),
 libssl-dev (>= 3.0),
 ninja-build,
 python3,
 qt6-base-dev (>= 6.8),
 qt6-l10n-tools,
 qt6-svg-dev,
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Homepage: https://linscp.org
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/99ecarvalho/linscp
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/99ecarvalho/linscp.git

Package: linscp
Architecture: any
Depends:
 qt6-svg-plugins,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 qt6-wayland,
Description: SFTP, SCP, FTP, WebDAV and S3 file-transfer client
 linscp transfers files between your computer and remote servers over
 SFTP, SCP, FTP (with TLS), WebDAV and S3. Its two-panel interface shows
 local and remote files side by side, with the same sessions, settings and
 scripting on Linux and Windows.
 .
 It synchronizes and compares directories, keeps a remote directory up to
 date, edits remote files, and runs commands on the server.
 .
 A WinSCP equivalent for Linux.
